sbook><name>KABUSHIKI KAISYA USHIOSOUGOU- GIZYUTSUKENKYUSYO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NEC CORPORATION</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SEKI, KYOHEI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TADA, AKIFUMI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SEKI KYOHEI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TADA AKIFUMI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SEKI, KYOHEI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TADA, AKIFUMI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>An excimer laser comprises a band-narrowing optical system (6) having an advantage that the oscillation center wavelength hardly varies with temperature and provided with a Littrow-mounted reflection-type diffraction grating (3) and a beam-expanding optical system (5) disposed on the light-incidence side of the reflection-type diffraction grating (5).  The beam expanding optical system (5) is composed of one or more beam expanding prism (11, 12) made of fluorite and one or more beam-expanding prism (13) made of synthetic quartz glass.  The rate of change of the oscillation center wavelength with respect to temperature change is made small by considering the number, arrangement, and direction of prisms (11, 12, 13).</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un laser excimer comprenant un système optique à rétrécissement de bande (6), dont l'avantage est que la longueur d'onde du centre d'oscillation varie à peine en fonction de la température. Le laser comporte un réseau de diffraction à réflexion de type Littrow (3) et un système optique dilatateur de faisceau (5) placé du côté lumière incidente du réseau de diffraction (5). Le système dilatateur de faisceau (5) comprend un ou plusieurs prismes dilatateurs (11, 12) en fluorine et un ou plusieurs prismes dilatateurs (13) en verre de quartz synthétique. Le taux de variation de la longueur d'onde du centre d'oscillation en fonction de la température est réduit grâce au nombre, à la configuration et la direction des prismes (11, 12, 13).</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>